    "name": "confirm",
    "description": "Tell the witness companion that undone asks are done, with evidence it checks itself. Confirm an ask in the same turn as its read-back, before calling it done: a later bulk confirm redoes the read-backs. For each ask cite evidence from a read-back made AFTER the ask was raised: {source:\"call\", command:<a piece of a tool call's input from this session>, excerpt:<words in that call's output, not in its input>}, or, for what only the user can witness (a layout), {source:\"user\", excerpt:<words the user typed>}. Only the first 1500 and last 2500 characters of an output are kept, so cite a short read-back (a grep or narrow query of the passage), never the middle of a long one. Every citation must check out or the ask stays undone; a claim is not evidence, nor is a subagent's report or its own calls (an Agent, Task or TaskOutput result): read back what it changed. When the user called an ask off, pass outcome \"dropped\" with those words as {source:\"user\"} evidence: the ask is then neither done nor undone, and never carried. Never drop an ask on your own judgement."
   }
